---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="About Us & Editorial Standards | SciCalcX Computational Suite" 
  description="Learn about the engineering team, mission, numerical accuracy standards, and architecture behind SciCalcX—an open-source scientific computational system and AI code tutor."
>
  <div class="w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8 font-sans">
    <!-- Page Header -->
    <div class="text-center md:text-left space-y-1.5 border-b border-brand-border/60 pb-4">
      <div class="text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-brand-blue-neon">
        Platform Profile &amp; Governance
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-text">
        About SciCalcX<span class="text-brand-blue">.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted">
        Bridging the gap between mathematical computation and interactive software compilation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Mission Card -->
    <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/40 rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4 shadow-xl backdrop-blur-sm">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-white font-mono flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-blue-neon"></span> Our Mission
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        SciCalcX was founded to solve a persistent frustration experienced by computer science and engineering students: the friction of switching between disconnected mathematical calculators, statistical analysis tools, and detached programming IDEs.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Our platform integrates high-precision numeric evaluation, linear algebra, calculus, and bitwise manipulation directly alongside an <strong>interactive AI coding tutor and compiler</strong>. Whether you are verifying matrix determinants for computer graphics, computing sample variance for experimental data, or writing C++ algorithms, SciCalcX delivers zero-latency results directly in your web browser.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Maintainers & Author Profiles (E-E-A-T) -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-white font-mono flex items-center gap-1.5 px-1">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400"></span> Engineering &amp; Editorial Team
      </h2>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/30 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white">Rishabh Raj Mahato</span>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-brand-blue-neon uppercase">Lead Developer</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Computer science student specializing in systems programming, compiler toolchains, and numerical computing. Lead architect of SciCalcX's token tokenizer, IEEE-754 precision sanitizer, and interactive bitboard simulator.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-brand-border/40 font-mono text-[10px]">
            <a href="https://github.com/RishabhDev817" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-blue-neon hover:underline">
              GitHub Profile &rarr;
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/30 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white">Riya</span>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-emerald-400 uppercase">Algorithm Research &amp; UX</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Developer focused on human-computer interaction, algorithm visualizers, and pedagogical content design. Curates our data structures curricula, descriptive statistics models, and educational tutorials.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-brand-border/40 font-mono text-[10px] text-brand-text-dim">
            Curriculum Lead
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial & Numerical Calculation Standards -->
    <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/40 rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-white font-mono flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-amber-400"></span> Calculation Accuracy &amp; Editorial Standards
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Accuracy is paramount in academic and scientific computing. We adhere to rigorous computational validation standards:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs text-brand-text-muted">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Precision Normalization:</strong> Floating-point calculations in standard binary engines often produce IEEE 754 precision artifacts (such as <code>0.1 + 0.2 = 0.30000000000000004</code>). SciCalcX applies custom decimal-normalization algorithms to guarantee exact human-readable representation up to 12 decimal figures.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Standardized Verification:</strong> Matrix transformations, cofactor determinants, and numerical Simpson's rule integrals are continuously tested against symbolic reference solutions and standard linear algebra benchmark datasets.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Editorial Integrity:</strong> All blog articles and handbooks are authored by engineering students, fact-checked against university curriculum specifications, and include reproducible C++ and Python code implementations.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-white">Client-Side Privacy:</strong> Your formulas, datasets, and compiled algorithms never leave your device. All computations run 100% client-side via modern WebAssembly and TypeScript engines.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Feature Ecosystem Grid -->
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-white font-mono flex items-center gap-1.5 px-1">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-blue"></span> Core Computational Ecosystem
      </h2>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <!-- Scientific & Matrix -->
        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/30 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-3 hover-glow transition-all">
          <div class="text-brand-blue-neon font-mono text-[10px] uppercase">Calculations &amp; Arrays</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">
            Advanced Calculator &amp; Matrix Suite
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Perform precision scientific evaluations, multi-line parenthesized formula calculations, and complex matrix operations (including determinant, inverse, transpose, and scalar arithmetic) with zero latency.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Calculus & Graphing -->
        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/30 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-3 hover-glow transition-all">
          <div class="text-brand-blue-neon font-mono text-[10px] uppercase">Calculus &amp; Geometry</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">
            Calculus &amp; Dynamic Graphing
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Evaluate integration limits, derivative approximations, sum sequences, and visualize mathematical coordinates overlays instantly using our high-performance graphing canvas system.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Bitboard & Base-N -->
        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/30 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-3 hover-glow transition-all">
          <div class="text-brand-blue-neon font-mono text-[10px] uppercase">Systems Programming</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">
            Interactive Programmer Bitboard
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Toggle binary bits interactively on a 32-bit visual grid, run bitwise operators (AND, OR, XOR, shifts), and automatically translate values across Hexadecimal, Decimal, Octal, and Binary representations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- AI Code Tutor & Compiler -->
        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/30 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-3 hover-glow transition-all">
          <div class="text-brand-blue-neon font-mono text-[10px] uppercase">Code &amp; Algorithms</div>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">
            AI Code Tutor &amp; Compiler Workspace
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
            Write, compile, and run code scripts (C++, Python, JS) directly in a pseudo-terminal console while receiving instant diagnostics, dynamic code explanations, and structured algorithm hints.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Tech Stack Profile -->
    <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-gray-dark/40 rounded-xl p-6 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-white font-mono flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand-blue"></span> Premium Web Architecture
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-brand-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        SciCalcX is built using the latest web standards to ensure accessibility, zero-dependency performance, and responsive mobile alignment.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 pt-2 font-mono text-[10px] text-center">
        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-black p-2.5 rounded hover-glow transition-all">
          <span class="text-brand-blue-neon block font-bold">Astro 6.x</span>
          Static Framework
        </div>
        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-black p-2.5 rounded hover-glow transition-all">
          <span class="text-brand-blue-neon block font-bold">Tailwind v4</span>
          Design Tokens
        </div>
        <div class="border border-brand-border bg-brand-black p-2.5 rounded hover-glow transition-all">
          <span class="text-brand-blue-neon block font-bold">TypeScript</span>
          Local Engines
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
